lz-disk-cleaner (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release v1.2.0
  * Bug fixes:
    - Fixed raw string literal (R"...") delimiter collision in regex patterns
    - Fixed int.toStdString() type error in helper program
    - Fixed custom cleanup dialog checkbox misalignment (dedicated column)
    - Fixed /persistent partition scanning returning empty results
    - Fixed du command exit code handling for permission-denied directories
    - Changed immutable system deployment data status from "safe" to "dangerous"
  * Performance improvements:
    - Replaced synchronous QDir::removeRecursively with async rm -rf via QProcess
    - Added CleanupThread class for non-blocking background deletion with progress feedback
    - Removed redundant du -sb pre-scan before each file deletion
    - Optimized getDirectorySize(): two-stage strategy (du -s fast → du -sb fallback)
  * UI improvements:
    - Custom cleanup tree widget restructured with dedicated checkbox column
    - Unknown directory sizes displayed as "未知" instead of hidden
    - Lowered minimum display threshold from 1MB to 4KB for scanned items

 -- LZ Disk Cleaner Team <support@lz-disk-cleaner.org>  Sat, 12 Apr 2026 14:30:00 +0800

lz-disk-cleaner (1.2.0-1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * New upstream release v1.2.0
  * Critical bug fixes:
    - Fixed whitelist rules not being applied during cleanup
    - Fixed "Keep Empty Directories" feature not working
    - Fixed "Full Protection" rules being ignored
    - Fixed "File Pattern Protection" not matching files
    - Fixed system log cleanup ignoring retention days setting
  * New features:
    - Whitelist checking with path matching (exact and prefix)
    - File pattern matching with wildcard support (*.lock, *.pid, etc.)
    - System-level whitelist auto-merge with user configuration
    - Detailed logging for whitelist checks
  * Improvements:
    - System logs now respect "Keep Days" setting (default: 7 days)
    - Journal logs now respect "Keep Days" setting
    - System snapshots now respect "Keep Count" setting (default: 3)
    - Added helper program logging for privileged operations
    - Better cleanup categorization (system logs, journal, snapshots)
  * Technical changes:
    - Added isPathInWhitelist() for path protection checking
    - Added isFileMatchPattern() for file pattern matching
    - Added cleanDirContent() to preserve directory structure
    - Refactored cleanup logic to apply whitelist rules
    - Fixed SYSTEM_LOGS using --system-logs option instead of direct deletion
    - Fixed JOURNAL_LOGS using --journal option with keepDays parameter

 -- LZ Disk Cleaner Team <support@lz-disk-cleaner.org>  Sat, 04 Apr 2026 12:45:00 +0800

